{
  "heading": "Store injection in every Yon language",
  "axis": "language",
  "body": "Choose one language. Copy server/application.json and that language's store and controller. GET /catalog queries the managed in-memory SQLite datasource. It returns [{\"amount\":42}]. In the controller language, you need no constructor of your own, no module manifest and no database library. The same query works with each SQL dialect. For real tables, bind values as parameters (do not paste them into the SQL text). Use the driver's placeholder syntax shown above. Run database schema migrations (changes to tables) outside controllers. These examples show bare Store provider injection. Store and Query methods bound to an entity work differently. They keep their explicit behavior context and authorization contract. The query text is one literal, and values go in the parameter list; Tachyon refuses query text built from pieces (`TY1325`).",
